<title>COTE D'IVOIRE: Ivory Coast raises cotton producer price.</title>
<headline>Ivory Coast raises cotton producer price.</headline>
<dateline>ABIDJAN 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ivory Coast's cabinet has increased the producer price of top grade seed cotton for the 1997/98 season to 200 CFA francs per kilo, from last season's 180 CFA.</p>
<p>A statement published in the government daily Fraternite-Matin said second grade cotton would be bought at 170 CFA francs, compared to 140 CFA for 1996/97.</p>
<p>It forecast 1996/97 production at 265,000 tonnes, compared to 218,000 in 1995/96. It said the government expected production of at least 280,000 tonnes for 1997/98.</p>
<p>It said yields for 1996/97 would be 13 percent higher that in 1995/96 and 39 percent higher than 1994/95, because of good rainfall and good husbandry.</p>
<p>--Abidjan newsroom +225 21 90 90</p>
</text>
